"\n## Unpack the images from super.img\n- When you build AOSP, host tools are also built.\n- Since the Super Image is a Sparse image, it must be converted to raw before unpacking.\n- The file system varies according to , and in the case of ext4, it can be mounted with .\n- If it's erofs, a separate tool (e.g., erofsfuse) is required for mounting.\n\n1. You need to convert the Sparse Image to a raw image.\n\n2. You need to extract the Super Image, which consists of multiple partitions.\n\n3. The file system of the images will appear as ext4, and you must add the offset option for mounting.\n"